WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.059
Veterans Day was originally Armistice
Day. President Woodrow Wilson set the day

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.540
aside in 1919 to honor the troops who
served in World War I.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.680
President Eisenhower expanded the
holiday to honor all living and still serving veterans.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.480
One way that American
veterans have continued to serve has

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.320
been by being politically active — by
being elected to Congress and the presidency.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.120
In the 2018 midterms, nearly
200 veterans ran for federal office

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.800
on election day. Veterans typically say
they want to join Congress to continue to

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.460
serve the public and to help protect our
democratic norms — through legislative,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.540
rather than military, means. It's
important to have veterans in Congress.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.570
They can bring a level of
defense expertise invaluable for shaping

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:50.250
national security policies. They tend to
ask more about when and how we use

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:54.120
military force; to conduct more oversight
of the executive branch; and to work to

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.080
see that the troops have the necessary
resources and training to operate

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:03.060
effectively and successfully. Having the
voice of veterans on the legislative "front lines"

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.400
is a substantive addition to our national debates.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.180
What do you think veterans bring to 
Congress? Let us know in your comments.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:15.260
Also, let us know what other topics you'd
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:20.540
and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for
more research and videos from AEI.

